From 870180b0b45bf132199bcb60349fb3bdb4d7107c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:11:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] patches: move banked PrismML source patches out of the
 generated series directory

patches/series/ is now GENERATED - 'series regen' rewrites it wholesale from git - so anything
hand-placed inside it is destroyed on the next regeneration.

It also broke the series' own completeness. The generated series excludes patches/series/ so
that the artifact converges (otherwise regenerating emits a patch containing the patch files,
committing that changes the series again, and there is no fixpoint). With the banked PrismML
patches living inside that excluded directory, the two commits that created them carried no
content outside it, dropped out of the series entirely, and 3103 lines of banked source would
have become unreproducible by replay - silently, with every check still green.

Moving them to patches/banked-source/ puts them back inside the series' coverage and makes the
distinction explicit: patches/series/ is our work and is generated; patches/banked-source/ is
other projects' patches, kept verbatim, never git am'd.

Taken-from: PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp@ternary-Q2_0_g128-lineage
Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110C
Measured-effect: file relocation only; patch contents byte-identical, no engine behaviour changed.
